  "ingredients": [
    "160 gram cauliflower (grated)",
    "3 tablespoon fresh chives (chopped)",
    "1/2 cup mozzarella cheese (grated)",
    "1/4 cup parmesan cheese (grated)",
    "1/2 cup cheddar cheese (grated)",
    "3 large egg",
    "1/2 teaspoon onion powder",
    "1/2 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/4 teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "2 large egg",
    "2 ounce prosciutto",
    "2 tablespoon hollandaise sauce (such as Trader Joe's)",
    "1.2 ounce smoked salmon",
    "1 ounce cream cheese",
    "1 tablespoon sour cream",
    "2 teaspoon fresh chives (chopped)",
    "1/2 teaspoon dried dill",
    "1/8 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1/8 teaspoon onion powder"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Get out the fresh cauliflower and chives. Break the cauliflower into florets. Finely chop the chives.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7112.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Grate the cauliflower and cheese using a food processor, and then remove the bowl from the base.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7127.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the chopped chives, eggs, and seasonings. Mix well.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7135.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat up a Belgian-style waffle maker and when it's ready, spoon the cauliflower mixture inside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7138.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Let cook, flip, and cook on the other side. This should take around 8–10 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/img_7145.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make these eggs Benedict–style by adding poached eggs, prosciutto, and hollandaise sauce; OR:",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/purplecauliflowerwaffleslong1.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the ingredients for the salmon spread to create a deliciously smoky, herby breakfast waffle. Both variations taste delicious. Enjoy!",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/breakfast-cauliflower-waffles/#wprm-recipe-51427-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
